    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0335" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1875: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-16T15:00:00+03:25">May 16, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. Reference to my No. 157, May 15, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>] p.m.
                    Minister of War informs me Soviet authorities have now given permission for
                    total of 1500 Iranian troops to proceed Rezaieh area. He stated that in his
                    opinion 5,000 troops are necessary to restore and maintain order in Rezaieh and
                    Tabriz and he is consequently requesting Soviet authorities to agree to the
                    sending of additional troops.</p>
                <p>Copy to Tabriz.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
